[36m(RolloutManager pid=45201)[0m [2026-09-29 07:21:23.035 rollout_manager] sglang_rollout.py:494 - Finish rollout: ['<|im_start|>user\nTim rides his bike back and forth to work for each of his 5 workdays.  His work is 20 miles away.  He also goes for a weekend bike ride of 200 miles.    If he can bike at 25 mph how much time does he spend biking a week?\nPut the final numeric answer in \\boxed{}.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\n\n</think>\n\nWe are given:\n\n- His work is 20 miles per day.\n- He goes for a weekend bike ride of 200 miles.\n- He rides this distance the **5 workdays** and **1 weekend trip**.\n- His biking speed is **25 mph**.\n- We need to find the **total time he spends biking in a week**.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Calculate the distance for work\n\nHe travels **20 miles per workday** for **5 days**:\n\n$$\n20 \\text{ miles/day} \\times 5 = 100 \\text{ miles}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Add weekend bike ride distance\n\n- 200 miles for the weekend.\n\nSo total distance:\n\n$$\n100 \\text{ miles} + 200 \\text{ miles} = 300 \\text{ miles}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Convert distance to time\n\nUse the formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Time} = \\frac{\\text{Distance}}{\\text{Speed}}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\text{Time} = \\frac{300 \\text{ miles}}{25 \\text{ mph}} = 12 \\text{ hours}\n$$\n\nSo, **he spends a total of 12 hours biking in a week.**\n\n---\n\n### ✅ Final Answer:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{12}\n$$<|im_end|>'], label: 16, reward: 0.0
